The desk merged **412 reports** into #4471 and marked it known: one bug, one fix. The reports
are not one bug. They are two. This page splits them, one ticket each.

## The two problems

| # | problem | reports | tenants | first seen | last seen |
|---|---------|---------|---------|------------|----------|
| 1 | [Parser reads dates month-first for day-first locales](https://github.com/8lueFox/kb-4471-what-it-shows/issues/1) | 379 | 11 | 2026-04-01 | 2026-10-04 |
| 2 | [booking-v3 hints MM/DD/YYYY but reads the date day-first](https://github.com/8lueFox/kb-4471-what-it-shows/issues/2) | 33 | 3 | 2026-04-17 | 2026-09-22 |

379 + 33 = 412: every report in #4471 has exactly one home. Five reports inside the parser
count are footnoted there — read differently in the desk's own notes, counted where
they're filed.

## How to tell them apart

- **Parser** (`src/lib/kb/causes.ts`, `causeOf`): the shared parser reads every date
  month-first. A day-first tenant's dates come out with month and day flipped. Any channel,
  any day-first tenant. This is the bug #4471 was opened for, and the queued fix is for it.
- **Hint**: the `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, people type what
  the hint tells them — month first — and the form then reads it the tenant's way, day-first.
  Same-looking symptom, different bug: only channel `form`, only `booking-v3` tenants
  (alder.physio de-DE, copper.studio es-ES, pale.harbour pt-PT).

<Callout kind="warn">
The hint bug will not be fixed by the queued parser fix. Until it is, those tenants'
form reports will keep arriving — and keep reading as "known".
</Callout>

## Why the desk saw one problem

- Intake tags disagree with the real cause in 38 of 412 reports: 23 tagged `hint` are
  parser, 15 tagged `parser` are hint. Tag, not tenant+form, drove the merge queue.
- Decision 0001 merges reports on subject lines alone. All of these subjects say the same
  thing ("wrong day", "dates mixed up"), so two bugs merged into one ticket. The decision
  accepted this ("engineering merges them later") — this page is that merge, done.

## What to do

Re-open #4471 into the two tickets above. The parser fix is already queued; the hint fix
is not, and every day it waits, the desk files its reports under a bug that cannot explain
them.

